    {
      "description": "Edit XLSX/CSV spreadsheets and typed game data in Unity. Validate tables and generate C# classes and runtime data.<p >Tested: Unity 6000.0.83f1 on Windows; Built-in sample scenes.</p><p >Samples require Unity uGUI and 2D Sprite. Addressables is optional and installed separately.</p><p >Includes English, Korean, Japanese, Simplified/Traditional Chinese, Spanish, French, German and Brazilian Portuguese UI and guides.</p><p >See the bundled guide for supported formulas and file-preservation limits. macOS, WebGL and IL2CPP runtime compatibility is not claimed.</p><p >Third-party sample artwork and fonts: see Third-Party Notices.txt.</p><p ><strong>Build and balance game data without leaving Unity.</strong></p><p ><strong>• Edit XLSX/CSV files with supported formulas, formatting, filters and charts.</strong></p><p ><strong>• Define typed game tables, validate records and generate C# classes and binary data.</strong></p><p ><strong>• Use drafts, backups and recovery, with optional Addressables and AI integrations.</strong></p><p ><strong>• Includes sample scenes and offline guides in nine languages.</strong></p><p ><strong>Supports a documented spreadsheet subset. XLS, macros and encrypted workbooks are not supported.</strong></p><p ><strong>Shared theme-aware controls and asset Inspectors; direct maximize/restore, with the document shelf below Unity’s console/status line.</strong></p><p >Promotional music: Cipher — Kevin MacLeod (incompetech.com). CC BY 3.0: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/3.0/ . Source: https://incompetech.com/music/royalty-free/index.html?isrc=USUAN1100844 . Excerpted, loudness adjusted and faded. Promotional videos only.</p>",
